00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:33.760
And we get all cold, shivery,

261
00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.720
and everything just starts feeling droopy.

262
00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:38.890
Hey, hey. Hey, easy.

263
00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.690
Why are you crying?

264
00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:44.240
It's just like really the opposite of what we're going for here.

265
00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.190
Crying helps me slow down,

266
00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.030
and obsess over the weight of life's problems.

267
00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.740
You know what? Let's, think about something else.

268
00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:56.790
How about we read some mind manuals, huh? Sounds fun.

269
00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.330
I've read most of them.

270
00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.120
Well, have you read this one? This seems interesting.

271
00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:03.290
"Long term memory retrieval, volume 47"?

272
00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.670
- No.  - A real page-turner!

273
00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:09.550
"Long term memory data selection via channel subgrouping"?

274
00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:12.260
See? Fun already! You lucky dog.

275
00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.000
You're reading these cool things.

276
00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.980
I got to go work. Life is so unfair.

277
00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:26.240
What can we do?

278
00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.690
We've only got capital to last a month, maybe two.

279
00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:30.430
If we can't find investors by then,

280
00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:32.360
we're going to have to lay people off.

281
00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:35.700
Mom! Dad! Come kiss me good night!

282
00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.080
- I know. I know.  - Be right there!

283
00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.380
We've got to land this, okay?

284
00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:43.750
Did you hear dad? He sounded really upset.

285
00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.010
What was that? Was it a bear? It's a bear!

286
00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:50.550
There are no bears in San Francisco.

287
00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.760
I saw a really hairy guy. He looked like a bear.

288
00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.140
I'm so jumpy. My nerves are shot.

289
00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.920
I don't want to hear about your nerves.

290
00:16:56.920 --> 00:16:57.820
I'll tell you what it is.

291
00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.660
This move has been a bust.

292
00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.070
That's what I've been telling you guys!

293
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.580
There are at least 37 things for Riley to be scared of right now.

294
00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.310
The smell alone is enough to make her gag.

295
00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.260
I can't believe mom and dad moved us here!

296
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.710
Look, I get it. You guys have concerns.

297
00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:11.170
But we've been through worse!

298
00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:12.570
Tell you what, let's make a list

299
00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:14.920
of all the things Riley should be happy about.

300
00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.720
Fine. Let's see, this house stinks, our room stinks.

301
00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.890
- Pizza is weird here.  - Our friends are back home.

302
00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.600
And all of our stuff is in the missing van!

303
00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.430
Come on. It could be worse.

304
00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.140
Yeah, Joy.

305
00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:27.060
We could be lying on the dirty floor. In a bag.

306
00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.020
Okay, I admit it, we had a rough start.

307
00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.460
But think of all the good things that...

308
00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:31.180
No, Joy.

309
00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:34.280
There's absolutely no reason for Riley to be happy right now.

310
00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.570
Let us handle this.

311
00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:38.070
I say we skip school tomorrow and lock ourselves in the bedroom.

312
00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.910
We have no clean clothes. I mean, no one should see us.

313
00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.700
Yeah, we could cry until we can't breathe.

314
00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:44.360
We should lock the door and scream that curse word we know.

315
00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.250
- It's a good one!  - Now hold on!

316
00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.290
Look, we all have our off days. You know...

317
00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.420
Hi, honey.

318
00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.350
The mom bad news train is pulling in.

319
00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.590
Still no moving Van.

320
00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.450
Now they're saying it won't be here till Tuesday,

321
00:17:58.450 --> 00:17:59.310
can you believe it?

322
00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.390
Where's dad?

323
00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:04.600
On the phone. This new venture is keeping him pretty busy.

324
00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.140
I rest my case!

325
00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.060
Your dad's a little stressed,

326
00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.160
you know, about getting his new company up and running.

327
00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.570
Now for a few well-placed withering scowls.

328
00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:16.690
I guess all I really want to say is,

329
00:18:16.810 --> 00:18:18.030
thank you.

330
00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:22.490
You know, through all this confusion you've stayed...

331
00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.330
Well, you've stayed our happy girl.

332
00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.210
Your dad's under a lot of pressure,

333
00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.170
but if you and I can keep smiling,

334
00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.910
it would be a big help.

335
00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.470
We can do that for him. Right?

336
00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.310
Yeah, sure.

337
00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.550
What did we do to deserve you?

338
00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.360
- Sweet dreams.  - Good night.

339
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.150
Well, you can't argue with mom. Happy it is.

340
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.400
Team Happy! Sounds great!

341
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.580
Totally behind you, Joy.

342
00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.900
Looks like we're going into rem.

343
00:18:58.900 --> 00:18:59.870
I got dream duty,

344
00:18:59.870 --> 00:19:01.860
so I'll take care of sending these to Long Term.

345
00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.650
Great day today, guys!

346
00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:06.120
Sleep well, Team Happy!

347
00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.550
All right, what's on tonight, Dream Production?

348
00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.250
Well, this is it. The new place.

349
00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.850
Come live with me, Riley.

350
00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.640
Somebody order a broccoli pizza?

351
00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.270
-Eat me!  -I'm organic!

352
00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:32.140
No! Who is in charge of programing down there?

353
00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:34.190
I know I'm not supposed to do this, but...

354
00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.500
We are not going to end the day like this.

355
00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:26.860
don't you worry.

356
00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:30.910
I'm gonna make sure that tomorrow is another great day.

357
00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.830
I promise.

358
00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.930
Hello! Did I wake you?

359
00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.050
Do you have to play that?

360
00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.350
Well, I have to practice.

361
00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.030
And I don't think of it as playing so much as hugging.

362
00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.730
First day of school! Very, very exciting.

363
00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.100
I was up late last night figuring out a new plan.

364
00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.230
Here it is! Fear.

365
00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.820
I need a list of all the possible negative outcomes

366
00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.110
on the first day at a new school.

367
00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:03.980
Way ahead of you there.

368
00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:05.450
Does anyone know how to spell "Meteor"?

369
00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.610
Disgust. Make sure Riley stands out today.

370
00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.910
But also blends in.

371
00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.780
When I'm through, Riley will look so good,

372
00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:12.950
the other kids will look at their own outfits and barf.

373
00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.120
"Joy." "Yes, Joy?"

374
00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.620
"You'll be in charge of the console,

375
00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.080
keeping Riley happy all day long.

376
00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.790
"And may I add I love your dress? It's adorable."

377
00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:20.250
"This old thing? Thank you so much.

378
00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:21.890
I love the way it twirls."

379
00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.600
Train of Thought! Right on schedule.

380
00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:28.550
Anger. Unload the daydreams.

381
00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.760
I ordered extra in case things get slow in class.

382
00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:31.800
It might come in handy.

383
00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:34.140
If this new school is full of boring, useless classes.

384
00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.810
Which it probably will be.

385
00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:39.520
Sadness. I have a super important job just for you.

386
00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.730
- Really?  - Follow me.

387
00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:46.280
- What are you doing?  - And there. Perfect!

388
00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.400
This is the circle of sadness.

389
00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:50.110
Your job is to make sure

390
00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:52.950
that all the sadness stays inside of it.

391
00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.790
So you want me to just stand here?

392
00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:59.080
Hey, it's not my place to tell you how to do your job.

393
00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:03.630
Just make sure that all the sadness stays in the circle!

394
00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:06.960
See? You're a pro at this! Isn't this fun?

395
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.170
- No.  - Atta girl.

396
00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:09.470
All right, everyone, fresh start.

397
00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:10.500
We are gonna have a good day,

398
00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.590
which will turn into a good week,

399
00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:12.550
which will turn into a good year,

400
00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:14.010
which turns into a good life!

401
00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.510
So, the big day!

402
00:22:15.510 --> 00:22:17.270
New school, new friends, huh?

403
00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.850
I know! I'm kind of nervous, but I'm mostly excited.

404
00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:21.270
How do I look? Do you like my shirt?

405
00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:22.980
Very cute!

406
00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.650
Are you gonna be okay? You want us to walk with you?

407
00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:26.570
Mom and dad? With us in public?

408
00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:28.030
- No thank you.  - I'm on it!

409
00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:30.620
Nope! I'm fine. Bye, mom. Bye, dad.

410
00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:32.450
Have a good day at school, Monkey.

411
00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:39.460
Have a great day, sweetheart!

412
00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:42.300
-That's crazy. It really is.  -That was so funny.

413
00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.600
Do you know what basketball game is coming up?

414
00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:47.210
Are you sure we want to do this?

415
00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:50.050
- In we go!  - Okay! Going in! Yes!

416
00:22:54.010 --> 00:22:55.510
Did you see her? Hello?

417
00:22:55.510 --> 00:22:57.970
Okay, we've got a group of cool girls at two o'clock.

418
00:22:57.970 --> 00:22:58.540
How do you know?

419
00:22:58.540 --> 00:23:00.390
Double ears pierced, infinity scarf.

420
00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:01.790
Is she wearing eye shadow?

421
00:23:01.790 --> 00:23:03.270
Yeah, we want to be friends with them.

422
00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:04.110
Let's go talk to them!

423
00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:05.730
Are you kidding? We're not talking to them.

424
00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:07.150
We want them to like us.

425
00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:08.570
Yeah. Wait, what?

426
00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:10.570
Almost finished with the potential disasters.

427
00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:14.070
Worst scenario is either quicksand, spontaneous combustion,

428
00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:15.740
or getting called on by the teacher.

429
00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:17.540
So as long as none of those happen...

430
00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.000
Okay, everybody. We have a new student in class today.

431
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.290
Are you kidding me? Out of the gate?

432
00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:23.540
This is not happening!

433
00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.250
Riley, would you like to tell us something about yourself?

434
00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:27.290
No!

435
00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:28.590
Pretend we can't speak English.

436
00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:29.810
don't worry. I got this.

437
00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:32.930
Okay.

438
00:23:32.930 --> 00:23:34.550
My name is Riley Andersen.

439
00:23:34.550 --> 00:23:37.810
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.

440
00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:42.440
And how about Minnesota?

441
00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:43.900
Can you tell us something about it?

442
00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:46.030
Well, you certainly get a lot more snow than we do.

443
00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.160
She's hilarious!

444
00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.280
Yeah, it gets pretty cold.

445
00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:55.780
The lake freezes over, and that's when we play hockey.

446
00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:58.120
I'm on a great team. We're called the Prairie Dogs.

447
00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:01.120
My friend Meg plays forward. And my dad's the coach.

448
00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.750
Pretty much everyone in my family skates.

449
00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:05.630
It's kind of a family tradition.

450
00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:07.430
We go out on the lake almost every weekend.

451
00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:13.130
Or we did, till I moved away.

452
00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:14.300
- Hey, what gives?  - Wait, what?

453
00:24:15.170 --> 00:24:16.920
Sadness! You touched a memory?

454
00:24:16.920 --> 00:24:18.600
We talked about this.

455
00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:20.310
Yeah, I know. I'm sorry.

456
00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:21.980
Get back in your circle.

457
00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:23.100
What's going on?

458
00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.190
- Why won't it eject?  - Get it out of there, Joy.

459
00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:27.730
We used to play tag and stuff.

460
00:24:27.730 --> 00:24:29.440
Cool kids whispering at three o'clock!

461
00:24:29.560 --> 00:24:30.650
- Did you see that look?  - No.

462
00:24:30.650 --> 00:24:31.990
They're judging us!

463
00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:35.570
Somebody help me! Grab that... everybody put...

464
00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:39.660
But everything's different now. Since we moved.

465
00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:45.260
No! We're crying! At school!

466
00:24:46.210 --> 00:24:48.760
What? Sadness! What are you doing?

467
00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:51.600
Oh, no! I'm sorry!

468
00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:54.840
It's a Core Memory!

469
00:24:54.840 --> 00:24:56.590
But it's blue.

470
00:24:58.180 --> 00:25:01.940
No! Wait! Stop it! No! No!

471
00:25:08.810 --> 00:25:10.020
Joy, no.

472
00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:11.520
That's a Core Memory!

473
00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:13.360
- Joy, wait!  - Stop it! Let go!

474
00:25:13.360 --> 00:25:15.210
The Core Memories!

475
00:25:29.920 --> 00:25:31.470
No, no, no, no!

476
00:25:44.680 --> 00:25:45.890
Thank you, Riley.

477
00:25:45.890 --> 00:25:48.480
I know it can be tough moving to a new place,

478
00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:51.020
but we're happy to have you here.

479
00:25:51.020 --> 00:25:53.190
All right, everyone, get out your history books

480
00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:55.320
and turn to chapter seven.

481
00:25:57.400 --> 00:25:59.420
Can I say that curse word now?

482
00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:23.570
No! One, two, three. Okay.

483
00:26:24.600 --> 00:26:26.020
I got them.

484
00:26:26.890 --> 00:26:28.350
Where are we?

485
00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:31.900
Long Term Memory? Wait...

486
00:26:37.810 --> 00:26:39.910
Goofball Island?

487
00:26:40.440 --> 00:26:44.790
Riley's Islands of Personality. They're all down!

488
00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:47.120
This is bad.

489
00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:49.620
We...we can fix this!

490
00:26:49.620 --> 00:26:51.540
We just have to get back to Headquarters,

491
00:26:51.540 --> 00:26:53.160
plug the Core Memories in,

492
00:26:53.160 --> 00:26:55.250
and Riley will be back to normal.

493
00:26:56.130 --> 00:26:58.330
Riley has no Core Memories.

494
00:26:58.330 --> 00:27:01.300
No Personality Islands and no...

495
00:27:01.510 --> 00:27:02.760
What? What is it?

496
00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:03.800
You.

497
00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:05.970
You're not in headquarters.

498
00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:08.430
Without you, Riley can't be happy.

499
00:27:09.270 --> 00:27:10.950
We got to get you back up there.

500
00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:12.990
I'm coming, Riley.

501
00:27:27.040 --> 00:27:28.370
So, as it turns out,

502
00:27:28.370 --> 00:27:30.490
the green trash can is not recycling,

503
00:27:30.490 --> 00:27:33.130
it's for greens. Like compost. And eggshells.

504
00:27:33.130 --> 00:27:34.710
And the blue one is recycling.

505
00:27:34.710 --> 00:27:35.760
And the black one is trash.

506
00:27:35.770 --> 00:27:36.920
Riley is acting so weird.

507
00:27:36.920 --> 00:27:37.960
Why is she acting so weird?

508
00:27:37.960 --> 00:27:40.380
What do you expect? All the islands are down.

509
00:27:40.380 --> 00:27:41.590
Joy would know what to do.

510
00:27:41.590 --> 00:27:42.720
That's it.

511
00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:45.640
Until she gets back, we just do what Joy would do!

512
00:27:45.640 --> 00:27:46.510
Great idea.

513
00:27:46.510 --> 00:27:48.470
Anger, Fear, Disgust,

514
00:27:48.470 --> 00:27:50.430
how are we supposed to be happy?

515
00:27:50.430 --> 00:27:52.200
Hey, Riley. I've got good news!

516
00:27:52.640 --> 00:27:55.480
I found a junior hockey league right here in San Francisco.

517
00:27:55.480 --> 00:27:56.420
And get this,

518
00:27:56.420 --> 00:27:58.390
Try-outs are tomorrow after school.

519
00:27:58.390 --> 00:27:59.530
What luck, right?

520
00:27:59.530 --> 00:28:01.030
- Hockey?  - What do we do?

521
00:28:01.030 --> 00:28:02.570
Guys, this is...

522
00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:03.950
You pretend to be Joy.

523
00:28:03.950 --> 00:28:06.530
Won't it be great to be back out on the ice?

524
00:28:07.910 --> 00:28:10.130
Yeah, that sounds fantastic.

525
00:28:10.870 --> 00:28:13.000
What was that? That wasn't anything like Joy!

526
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.300
- Because I'm not Joy.  - Yeah, no kidding.

527
00:28:17.340 --> 00:28:18.710
Did you guys pick up on that?

528
00:28:18.710 --> 00:28:20.710
- Something's wrong.  - Totally.

529
00:28:20.710 --> 00:28:22.010
Should we ask her?

530
00:28:22.010 --> 00:28:22.680
Let's probe.

531
00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:24.880
But keep it subtle, so she doesn't notice.

532
00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:27.220
So, how was the first day of school?

533
00:28:27.220 --> 00:28:28.430
She's probing us.

534
00:28:28.430 --> 00:28:29.970
I'm done. You pretend to be Joy.

535
00:28:29.970 --> 00:28:31.730
What? Okay.

536
00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:35.730
It was fine, I guess. I don't know.

537
00:28:35.730 --> 00:28:38.560
Very smooth. That was just like Joy.

538
00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:40.730
Something is definitely going on.

539
00:28:40.730 --> 00:28:43.190
She's never acted like this before. What should we do?

540
00:28:43.190 --> 00:28:44.900
We're going to find out what's happening.

541
00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:46.240
But we'll need support.

542
00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:47.330
Signal the husband.

543
00:28:51.120 --> 00:28:53.030
With a nice pass over to Reeves,

544
00:28:53.030 --> 00:28:54.660
comes across...And nice!

545
00:28:58.130 --> 00:28:59.260
She's looking at us.

546
00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:02.420
- What did she say?  - What?

547
00:29:02.420 --> 00:29:03.920
Sorry, sir. No one was listening.

548
00:29:03.920 --> 00:29:06.380
Is it garbage night? We left the toilet seat up?

549
00:29:06.380 --> 00:29:08.260
What? What is it, woman? What?

550
00:29:08.260 --> 00:29:10.510
He's making that stupid face again.

551
00:29:10.510 --> 00:29:12.430
I could strangle him right now.

552
00:29:12.430 --> 00:29:13.680
Signal him again.

553
00:29:17.190 --> 00:29:19.110
So, Riley, how was school?

554
00:29:19.110 --> 00:29:21.070
- You got to be kidding me!  - Seriously?

555
00:29:21.070 --> 00:29:22.490
For this we gave up that

556
00:29:22.490 --> 00:29:24.330
Brazilian helicopter pilot?

557
00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:26.280
Move! I'll be Joy.

558
00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:28.200
School was great, all right?

559
00:29:28.200 --> 00:29:30.380
Riley. Is everything okay?

560
00:29:31.700 --> 00:29:33.450
Sir, she just rolled her eyes at us.

561
00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:35.120
What is her deal?

562
00:29:35.120 --> 00:29:36.870
All right, make a show of force.

563
00:29:36.870 --> 00:29:38.460
I don't want to have to put the foot Down.

564
00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:40.460
No, not the foot!

565
00:29:40.460 --> 00:29:42.800
Riley, I do not like this new attitude.

566
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:44.500
I'll show you attitude, old man.

567
00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:45.800
No. No, no, no! Stay happy!

568
00:29:46.550 --> 00:29:48.930
What is your problem? Just leave me alone!

569
00:29:48.930 --> 00:29:50.720
Sir, reporting high levels of sass!

570
00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:52.640
Take it to defcon two.

571
00:29:52.640 --> 00:29:54.690
You heard that, gentlemen. Defcon two.

572
00:29:55.990 --> 00:29:56.750
Listen, young lady,

573
00:29:56.750 --> 00:29:59.650
I don't know where this disrespectful attitude came from...

574
00:29:59.650 --> 00:30:02.570
You want a piece of this, pops? Come and get it!

575
00:30:02.570 --> 00:30:04.150
Yeah, well... well...

576
00:30:04.150 --> 00:30:06.530
Here it comes. Prepare the foot!

577
00:30:07.990 --> 00:30:09.500
Keys to safety position.

578
00:30:11.320 --> 00:30:12.910
Ready to launch on your command, sir!

579
00:30:15.580 --> 00:30:17.220
Just shut up!

580
00:30:18.160 --> 00:30:19.830
Fire!

581
00:30:19.830 --> 00:30:23.710
That's it! Go to your room! Now!

582
00:30:26.840 --> 00:30:29.850
The foot is down! The foot is down!

583
00:30:31.010 --> 00:30:34.850
Good job, gentlemen. That could have been a disaster.

584
00:30:35.260 --> 00:30:36.930
Well, that was a disaster.

585
00:30:40.100 --> 00:30:42.820
Come fly with me, Gatinha.

586
00:30:55.200 --> 00:30:57.950
We're going to walk out there? On that?

587
00:30:57.950 --> 00:30:59.790
It's the quickest way back.

588
00:30:59.790 --> 00:31:01.920
But it's right over the Memory Dump.

589
00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:04.310
If we fall, we'll be forgotten forever.

590
00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:06.390
We have to do this for Riley.

591
00:31:06.390 --> 00:31:08.770
- Just follow my footsteps.  - Okay.

592
00:31:08.770 --> 00:31:12.850
It's not that high. It's totally fine...

593
00:31:30.070 --> 00:31:33.130
So, things got a little out of hand downstairs.

594
00:31:34.070 --> 00:31:35.990
Do you want to talk about it?

595
00:31:37.040 --> 00:31:39.340
Come on, where's my happy girl?

596
00:31:40.750 --> 00:31:41.880
Monkey.

597
00:31:42.830 --> 00:31:44.840
He's trying to start up Goofball.

598
00:31:46.070 --> 00:31:47.360
Come on!

599
00:31:59.750 --> 00:32:01.340
Go back! Run, run, run!

600
00:32:29.110 --> 00:32:30.490
What...

601
00:32:45.750 --> 00:32:48.590
I get it. You need some alone time.

602
00:32:51.510 --> 00:32:52.850
We'll talk later.

603
00:32:56.310 --> 00:32:58.150
We have a Major problem.

604
00:32:58.730 --> 00:33:00.240
Joy, where are you?

605
00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:03.980
We lost Goofball Island.

606
00:33:03.980 --> 00:33:05.570
That means she can lose

607
00:33:05.580 --> 00:33:08.780
friendship and hockey and honesty and family.

608
00:33:08.780 --> 00:33:11.400
You can fix this, right, Joy?

609
00:33:11.410 --> 00:33:12.500
I...

610
00:33:13.700 --> 00:33:15.070
I don't know.

611
00:33:15.080 --> 00:33:17.260
But we have to try. Okay, come on.

612
00:33:18.540 --> 00:33:20.620
Riley's gone to sleep.

613
00:33:20.620 --> 00:33:24.710
Which is a good thing. When you think about it because

614
00:33:24.710 --> 00:33:26.960
nothing else bad can happen while she's asleep.

615
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:29.130
We'll be back to headquarters before she wakes up.

616
00:33:29.130 --> 00:33:31.760
We'll just go across Friendship Island.

617
00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:35.550
We'll never make it.

618
00:33:35.550 --> 00:33:36.890
No! No, no, no!

619
00:33:36.890 --> 00:33:38.350
Don't obsess over the weight of life's problems.

620
00:33:38.350 --> 00:33:40.220
Remember the funny movie where the dog dies?

621
00:33:40.230 --> 00:33:42.810
Sadness, we don't have time for this.

622
00:33:42.810 --> 00:33:46.400
We'll just have to go around. Take the scenic route.

623
00:33:46.400 --> 00:33:48.860
Wait, Joy, you could get lost in there!

624
00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:50.480
Think positive!

625
00:33:50.490 --> 00:33:54.130
Okay. I'm positive you will get lost in there.

626
00:33:54.660 --> 00:33:56.410
That's long term memory.

627
00:33:56.410 --> 00:33:59.040
An endless Warren of corridors and shelves.

628
00:33:59.040 --> 00:34:01.580
I read about it in the manuals.

629
00:34:01.580 --> 00:34:04.620
The manuals? The manuals!

630
00:34:04.630 --> 00:34:06.540
- You read the manuals!  - Yeah.

631
00:34:06.540 --> 00:34:08.750
So you know the way back to headquarters!

632
00:34:08.750 --> 00:34:09.840
I guess.

633
00:34:12.880 --> 00:34:14.010
You are my map!

634
00:34:14.430 --> 00:34:17.720
Let's go! Lead on, my map! Show me where we're going!

635
00:34:17.720 --> 00:34:21.520
Okay. Only I'm too sad to walk.

636
00:34:21.520 --> 00:34:24.620
Just give me a few...Hours.

637
00:34:26.060 --> 00:34:27.270
Which way? Left?

638
00:34:27.270 --> 00:34:28.480
Right.

639
00:34:28.980 --> 00:34:32.490
No. I mean, go left. I said left was right. Like "Correct."

640
00:34:32.490 --> 00:34:33.740
Okay.

641
00:34:33.740 --> 00:34:35.950
This actually feels kind of nice.

642
00:34:35.950 --> 00:34:37.060
Okay, here we go!

643
00:34:37.060 --> 00:34:39.370
We'll be back to headquarters before morning.

644
00:34:39.370 --> 00:34:43.050
We can do it! This will be easy! This is working!

645
00:34:46.460 --> 00:34:49.290
This is not working. Are we getting close?

646
00:34:49.290 --> 00:34:50.880
Yeah, just another right.

647
00:34:51.460 --> 00:34:56.470
And...A left and then another...Left and...

648
00:34:56.470 --> 00:34:58.930
Are you sure you know where we're going?

649
00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:01.780
Because we seem to be walking away from headquarters.

650
00:35:02.560 --> 00:35:04.450
Riley's awake.

651
00:35:08.520 --> 00:35:10.060
Don't touch. Remember?

652
00:35:10.060 --> 00:35:12.650
If you touch them, they stay sad.

653
00:35:12.650 --> 00:35:16.200
Sorry, I won't. Starting now.

654
00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:18.570
I can't take much more of this.

655
00:35:18.570 --> 00:35:20.160
Forget them!

656
00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:22.760
- Mind workers!  - But, Joy, we're almost...

657
00:35:23.870 --> 00:35:26.750
Phone numbers. We don't need all these. They're in her phone.

658
00:35:26.750 --> 00:35:28.890
- Excuse me, hi.  - Just forget all of that. Please. Forget it!

659
00:35:30.340 --> 00:35:32.000
- I need to find Friendship Island.  - Look at this.

660
00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:33.500
Four years of piano lessons.

661
00:35:33.510 --> 00:35:34.840
Yeah, it looks pretty faded.

662
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:36.670
You know what? Save Chopsticks and Heart and Soul,

663
00:35:36.670 --> 00:35:37.800
get rid of the rest.

664
00:35:38.300 --> 00:35:40.010
- Are you...  - U.S. Presidents. What do you think?

665
00:35:40.010 --> 00:35:42.260
Yeah, just keep Washington, Lincoln and the fat one.

666
00:35:42.260 --> 00:35:44.520
- Forget 'em!  - Hey! You can't throw those away!

667
00:35:44.520 --> 00:35:45.930
Those are perfectly good memories.

668
00:35:45.930 --> 00:35:48.270
The names of every "Cutie Pie Princess" Doll?

669
00:35:48.270 --> 00:35:49.880
Yes! That is critical information!

670
00:35:49.880 --> 00:35:51.440
Glitterstorm, Honeypants...

671
00:35:51.440 --> 00:35:52.780
Forget 'em!

672
00:35:57.450 --> 00:35:58.740
Hey! Bring those back!

673
00:35:58.740 --> 00:36:01.030
They're in the dump. Nothing comes back from the dump.

674
00:36:01.030 --> 00:36:02.700
Yeah. Look, lady, this is our job, okay?

675
00:36:02.700 --> 00:36:05.160
When Riley doesn't care about a memory, it fades.

676
00:36:05.160 --> 00:36:06.580
- Fades?  - Happens to the best of them.

677
00:36:06.580 --> 00:36:10.460
Yeah, except for this bad boy. This one will never fade.

678
00:36:10.670 --> 00:36:12.630
- Tripledent gum  - Will make you smile

679
00:36:12.630 --> 00:36:14.000
The song from the gum commercial?

680
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:14.950
You know, sometimes we send

681
00:36:14.950 --> 00:36:16.510
that one up to headquarters for no reason.

682
00:36:16.510 --> 00:36:18.970
It just plays in Riley's head over and over again.

683
00:36:18.970 --> 00:36:20.800
Like a million times!

684
00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:21.930
Let's watch it again!

685
00:36:21.930 --> 00:36:23.550
Tripledent gum

686
00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:25.170
Yeah, I know. We all know the song.

687
00:36:25.170 --> 00:36:26.600
Okay. Yeah, real catchy. Okay.

688
00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:27.850
Hey, what do you think? Should we do it?

689
00:36:27.850 --> 00:36:28.890
Yeah!

690
00:36:28.890 --> 00:36:30.480
Okay, here we go!

691
00:36:33.570 --> 00:36:34.730
Tripledent gum

692
00:36:34.730 --> 00:36:36.490
What the... this again?

693
00:36:37.740 --> 00:36:40.170
Wait! Do you know how to get to Friendship Island?

694
00:36:40.410 --> 00:36:41.490
Tripledent gum

695
00:36:41.490 --> 00:36:42.450
Do you like it there?

696
00:36:42.450 --> 00:36:44.740
Did you feel any earthquakes? Is the bridge cool?

697
00:36:44.740 --> 00:36:47.580
Yeah, it's good. What happened with the playoffs?

698
00:36:47.580 --> 00:36:48.660
We won the first game.

699
00:36:48.660 --> 00:36:50.960
Coach says we might actually go to the finals this year.

700
00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:53.920
And we've got this new girl on the team. She's so cool.

701
00:36:53.920 --> 00:36:55.500
She did not just say that.

702
00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:58.380
A new girl? Meg has a new friend already?

703
00:36:58.760 --> 00:37:00.050
Hey, hey! Stay happy!

704
00:37:00.050 --> 00:37:02.180
We do not want to lose any more islands here, guys!

705
00:37:02.390 --> 00:37:04.550
We can pass the puck to each other without even looking.

706
00:37:04.560 --> 00:37:06.010
It's like mind reading!

707
00:37:06.010 --> 00:37:07.390
You like to read minds, Meg?

708
00:37:07.390 --> 00:37:09.310
I got something for you to read, right here!

709
00:37:09.310 --> 00:37:10.730
Let's just be calm for one second!

710
00:37:11.560 --> 00:37:13.190
- I heard they have parrots...  - I've got to go.

711
00:37:13.190 --> 00:37:14.660
- What?  - I got to go!

712
00:37:15.940 --> 00:37:20.240
Okay, could you just please tell me which way is... oh, no!

713
00:37:23.700 --> 00:37:25.840
Friendship Island! What?

714
00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.420
Not friendship.

715
00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:48.850
Riley loved that one. And now it's gone.

716
00:37:48.850 --> 00:37:52.570
Goodbye, friendship. Hello, loneliness.

717
00:37:56.900 --> 00:37:58.910
We'll just have to go the long way.

718
00:37:59.650 --> 00:38:04.120
Yeah. The long, long, long, long way.

719
00:38:04.990 --> 00:38:06.410
I'm ready.

720
00:38:07.620 --> 00:38:09.970
There's got to be a better way.

721
00:38:12.410 --> 00:38:13.580
Look at you!

722
00:38:14.880 --> 00:38:17.500
I will take you, but not you.

723
00:38:17.500 --> 00:38:19.630
Who am I kidding? I can't leave you.

724
00:38:19.960 --> 00:38:21.840
Hello!

725
00:38:21.840 --> 00:38:23.140
Wait! Hey! Wait!

726
00:38:25.430 --> 00:38:27.110
Wait! Stop!

727
00:38:35.770 --> 00:38:36.900
Excuse me.

728
00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:40.440
- I was looking for...  - Diversion!

729
00:38:40.440 --> 00:38:42.400
- What?  - So long, sucker!

730
00:38:43.950 --> 00:38:45.110
I hurt all over.

731
00:38:45.110 --> 00:38:46.990
Wait. I know you.

732
00:38:46.990 --> 00:38:49.180
No, you don't. I get that a lot.

733
00:38:49.180 --> 00:38:50.620
I look like a lot of people.

734
00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:52.080
No, no, no. I do.

735
00:38:52.080 --> 00:38:54.870
Bing Bong! Riley's imaginary friend!

736
00:38:54.870 --> 00:38:57.420
- You really do know me?  - Well, of course!

737
00:38:57.420 --> 00:38:58.900
Riley loved playing with you!

738
00:38:58.910 --> 00:39:00.040
You two are best friends!

739
00:39:00.050 --> 00:39:02.590
You would know. We're trying to get back to headquarters.

740
00:39:02.590 --> 00:39:04.840
Headquarters? You guys are from headquarters?

741
00:39:04.840 --> 00:39:08.010
Well, yeah. I'm Joy. This is Sadness.

742
00:39:08.010 --> 00:39:09.760
You're Joy? The Joy?

743
00:39:09.760 --> 00:39:11.430
What the heck are you doing out here?

744
00:39:11.430 --> 00:39:13.600
That's a good question. You want to answer that, Sadness?

745
00:39:13.600 --> 00:39:16.640
Without you, Riley won't ever be happy.

746
00:39:16.650 --> 00:39:19.110
We can't have that. We got to get you back.

747
00:39:19.110 --> 00:39:21.190
I'll tell you what. Follow me!

748
00:39:21.190 --> 00:39:22.280
Thank you!

749
00:39:22.280 --> 00:39:23.990
It is so great to see you again.

750
00:39:23.990 --> 00:39:26.280
I gotta tell you, I am such a huge fan of your work.

751
00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:29.370
Do you remember when you and Riley were in a band?

752
00:39:29.370 --> 00:39:31.280
I went to all of your concerts.

753
00:39:31.290 --> 00:39:32.790
Yeah, I blow a mean nose.

754
00:39:32.790 --> 00:39:34.410
Watching you play tag was such a treat.

755
00:39:34.410 --> 00:39:35.790
Two-time world champ.

756
00:39:35.790 --> 00:39:37.500
And remember your rockets?

757
00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:39.830
Of course! It runs on song power!

758
00:39:39.840 --> 00:39:41.340
That's right! Your theme song!

759
00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:42.800
Who's your friend who likes to play?*

760
00:39:42.800 --> 00:39:44.130
Bing bong bing bong

761
00:39:44.130 --> 00:39:45.550
His rocket makes you yell "Hooray!"

762
00:39:45.550 --> 00:39:47.340
- Bing bong, bing bong  - Bing bong, bing bong

763
00:39:47.340 --> 00:39:49.760
What exactly are you supposed to be?

764
00:39:49.760 --> 00:39:52.560
You know, it's unclear. I'm mostly cotton candy.

765
00:39:52.560 --> 00:39:57.350
But shape-wise I'm part cat, part elephant, part dolphin.

766
00:39:57.350 --> 00:39:58.310
Dolphin?

767
00:40:01.320 --> 00:40:03.140
You got to remember, when Riley was three,

768
00:40:03.140 --> 00:40:04.360
animals were all the rage.

769
00:40:04.360 --> 00:40:06.320
The cow goes moo. The horse goes neigh.

770
00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:08.030
That's all people talked about back then.

771
00:40:08.030 --> 00:40:10.620
Yeah. Yeah. I guess that's true. What are you doing out here?

772
00:40:10.620 --> 00:40:14.120
Well, there's not much call for imaginary friends lately.

773
00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:16.670
So I, you know...

774
00:40:18.290 --> 00:40:20.710
Hey, hey. Don't be sad.

775
00:40:20.710 --> 00:40:22.880
Tell you what. When I get back up to headquarters,

776
00:40:22.880 --> 00:40:24.920
I'll make sure Riley remembers you.

777
00:40:24.920 --> 00:40:27.340
- You will?  - Of course! She'd love that.

778
00:40:28.380 --> 00:40:30.930
This is the greatest day of my life!

779
00:40:34.770 --> 00:40:35.860
Are you okay?

780
00:40:36.980 --> 00:40:39.310
- Hey, what's going on?  - I cry candy.

781
00:40:39.310 --> 00:40:41.520
Try the caramel. It's delicious.

782
00:40:43.570 --> 00:40:45.150
- Here, use this.  - Thanks!

783
00:40:45.150 --> 00:40:46.280
Hold on, wait a second.

784
00:40:49.740 --> 00:40:51.880
It always gets stuck at the bottom.

785
00:40:54.450 --> 00:40:57.580
Here. What? It's imaginary.

786
00:40:57.580 --> 00:40:58.700
Thanks. This will make it

787
00:40:58.700 --> 00:41:00.670
a lot easier to walk back to headquarters.

788
00:41:00.670 --> 00:41:02.500
Walk? We're not walking.

789
00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:04.670
We're taking the train of thought!

790
00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:08.130
The train, of course!

791
00:41:08.130 --> 00:41:10.720
That is so much faster! But how do we catch it?

792
00:41:10.720 --> 00:41:12.510
Well, it kind of goes all over the place,

793
00:41:12.510 --> 00:41:14.970
but there is a station in Imagination Land.

794
00:41:14.970 --> 00:41:17.720
I know a shortcut. Come on, this way!

795
00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:19.980
I am so glad we ran into you!

796
00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:23.270
The station is right through here. After you.

797
00:41:23.270 --> 00:41:24.690
- Joy.  - What?

798
00:41:24.690 --> 00:41:26.500
I read about this place in the manual.

799
00:41:26.500 --> 00:41:27.900
We shouldn't go in there.

800
00:41:27.900 --> 00:41:30.490
Bing bong says it's the quickest way to headquarters.

801
00:41:30.490 --> 00:41:32.740
No, but, Joy, this is abstract thought.

802
00:41:32.740 --> 00:41:34.050
What are you talking about?

803
00:41:34.050 --> 00:41:36.370
I go in here all the time. It's a shortcut, you see?

804
00:41:36.370 --> 00:41:40.950
D-a-n-g-e-r. Shortcut. I'll prove it to you.

805
00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:43.830
Look at me. I'm closer to the station

806
00:41:43.830 --> 00:41:46.210
because I'm taking the shortcut.

807
00:41:46.960 --> 00:41:48.460
Let's go around. This way.

808
00:41:48.460 --> 00:41:50.300
Almost there!

809
00:41:51.090 --> 00:41:53.720
If you want to walk the long way, go for it.

810
00:41:53.720 --> 00:41:55.760
But Riley needs to be happy.

811
00:41:55.760 --> 00:41:56.790
I'm not missing that train.

812
00:41:56.790 --> 00:41:58.600
Bing bong knows what he's doing.

813
00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:00.560
He's part dolphin. They're very smart.

814
00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:02.320
Well, I guess.

815
00:42:05.440 --> 00:42:07.290
- What did you get?  - I don't know.

816
00:42:21.120 --> 00:42:24.500
Okay, what abstract concept are we trying to comprehend today?

817
00:42:25.080 --> 00:42:26.830
Loneliness.

818
00:42:26.840 --> 00:42:28.460
Looks like there's something in there.

819
00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:30.960
I'm going to turn it on for a minute and burn out the gunk.

820
00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:33.590
What did I tell you? You'll be at headquarters in no time.

821
00:42:34.590 --> 00:42:36.260
Hey, would you look at that?

822
00:42:37.850 --> 00:42:40.030
- What's happening?  - Oh, no, they turned it on.

823
00:42:40.720 --> 00:42:41.980
Never seen this before.

824
00:42:44.730 --> 00:42:47.700
My face! My beautiful face!

825
00:42:48.400 --> 00:42:49.860
- What is going on?  - We're abstracting!

826
00:42:49.860 --> 00:42:51.160
There are four stages.

827
00:42:51.160 --> 00:42:54.030
This is the first: Non-objective fragmentation!

828
00:42:54.030 --> 00:42:55.200
All right. Do not panic.

829
00:42:55.200 --> 00:42:57.710
What is important is that we all stay together.

830
00:42:59.120 --> 00:43:01.740
We're in the second stage. We're deconstructing!

831
00:43:01.750 --> 00:43:02.840
Run!

832
00:43:04.620 --> 00:43:06.090
I can't feel my legs!

833
00:43:06.710 --> 00:43:07.920
There they are.

834
00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:09.220
Come here, me!

835
00:43:10.800 --> 00:43:12.150
We've got to get out of here

836
00:43:12.150 --> 00:43:14.920
before we're nothing but shape and color!

837
00:43:14.930 --> 00:43:16.510
We'll get stuck here forever!

838
00:43:16.510 --> 00:43:18.340
Stuck? Why did we come in here?

839
00:43:18.350 --> 00:43:21.010
I told you, it's a shortcut!

840
00:43:21.010 --> 00:43:22.690
The train!

841
00:43:26.350 --> 00:43:30.150
Oh, no. We're two-dimensional! That's stage three!

842
00:43:30.150 --> 00:43:31.190
We're getting nowhere!

843
00:43:31.190 --> 00:43:34.360
- Depth! I'm lacking depth!  - Come on.

844
00:43:37.410 --> 00:43:38.740
We can't fit.

845
00:43:38.740 --> 00:43:42.660
Oh, no, we're nonfigurative. This is the last stage!

846
00:43:42.660 --> 00:43:44.500
We're not going to make it!

847
00:43:46.330 --> 00:43:49.960
Wait! We're two-dimensional. Fall on your face!

848
00:44:00.720 --> 00:44:02.730
Stop! Stop!

849
00:44:03.930 --> 00:44:07.140
No! I thought you said that was a shortcut.

850
00:44:07.140 --> 00:44:10.150
I did, but wow, we should not have gone in there.

851
00:44:10.150 --> 00:44:12.120
That was dangerous! They really should put up a sign.

852
00:44:12.360 --> 00:44:13.450
How long until the next train?

853
00:44:13.570 --> 00:44:17.320
Who knows. But don't worry. There's another station. That way.

854
00:44:17.320 --> 00:44:18.670
The train always stops there.

855
00:44:18.680 --> 00:44:20.490
Right before it goes to headquarters.

856
00:44:20.490 --> 00:44:22.530
If we hurry, we can catch it.

857
00:44:22.530 --> 00:44:24.910
This isn't another one of your shortcuts, is it?

858
00:44:25.750 --> 00:44:27.370
Yeah!

859
00:44:27.370 --> 00:44:29.210
Is there really another station?

860
00:44:29.210 --> 00:44:30.470
Through there.

861
00:44:32.590 --> 00:44:35.180
Welcome to Imagination Land!

862
00:44:35.380 --> 00:44:37.510
- Imagination land?  - Sure!

863
00:44:37.510 --> 00:44:39.930
I come here all the time. I'm practically the mayor.

864
00:44:39.930 --> 00:44:42.760
Hey, you guys hungry? There's French Fry Forest!

865
00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:45.100
- Delicious.  - No way!

866
00:44:45.100 --> 00:44:47.810
Check it out! Trophy Town!

867
00:44:47.810 --> 00:44:50.980
Medals! Ribbons! Everyone's a winner!

868
00:44:51.650 --> 00:44:53.690
I won first place!

869
00:44:53.690 --> 00:44:56.530
- Me too!  - Participation award.

870
00:44:56.530 --> 00:45:00.030
Wait, is that... Sadness, look, it's Cloud Town!

871
00:45:00.030 --> 00:45:02.070
That is my favorite!

872
00:45:02.070 --> 00:45:03.530
It's so soft!

873
00:45:03.530 --> 00:45:05.330
Let me try.

874
00:45:05.330 --> 00:45:07.200
Hey! What's the big idea?

875
00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:10.000
You better fix that wall, or else you're in big troub...

876
00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:13.500
Oh, no! Lava!

877
00:45:14.920 --> 00:45:16.920
Imagination Land is the best!

878
00:45:18.050 --> 00:45:20.880
Is it all going to be so interactive?

879
00:45:20.880 --> 00:45:23.260
Hey, look! The House of Cards!

880
00:45:23.260 --> 00:45:25.680
Wait. Hang on just a minute.

881
00:45:25.680 --> 00:45:27.220
- Your rocket!  - Yeah.

882
00:45:27.220 --> 00:45:29.020
I stashed it in there for safekeeping,

883
00:45:29.020 --> 00:45:31.530
and now I'm all set to take Riley to the moon!

884
00:45:32.650 --> 00:45:34.520
- I'm sorry.  - Great.

885
00:45:34.520 --> 00:45:36.690
I love Imagination Land.

886
00:45:36.690 --> 00:45:39.530
Isn't it great? And there's always something new, like...

887
00:45:41.950 --> 00:45:43.360
Who the heck is that?

888
00:45:43.370 --> 00:45:44.780
Imaginary boyfriend.

889
00:45:44.780 --> 00:45:46.700
I would die for Riley.

890
00:45:47.450 --> 00:45:49.670
- I've never seen him before.  - I live in Canada.

891
00:45:50.410 --> 00:45:52.870
Anyway, this way. Through Preschool World!

892
00:45:52.880 --> 00:45:54.000
We're nearly to the train!

893
00:45:54.700 --> 00:45:56.170
Riley, here we come!

894
00:45:58.300 --> 00:46:01.880
This should be fun! New team, new friends.

895
00:46:01.880 --> 00:46:03.260
These kids look pretty good,

896
00:46:03.260 --> 00:46:04.970
considering they're from San Francisco.

897
00:46:04.970 --> 00:46:06.350
Okay, Andersen, you're up!

898
00:46:06.350 --> 00:46:09.470
- Got to go.  - Okay. Good luck, sweetie!

899
00:46:09.470 --> 00:46:10.730
Luck isn't going to help us now.

900
00:46:10.730 --> 00:46:12.560
If she tries to use Hockey Island, it's going down.

901
00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:15.980
Which is why I've recalled every hockey memory I can think of.

902
00:46:15.980 --> 00:46:18.820
One of these has got to work in place of the core memory.

903
00:46:18.820 --> 00:46:20.330
- She's about to play!  - Hurry!

904
00:46:27.990 --> 00:46:30.620
We did it, gang! It's working!

905
00:46:33.580 --> 00:46:37.920
Line change! Line change! Change it up!

906
00:46:42.720 --> 00:46:44.110
No! No!

907
00:46:49.470 --> 00:46:51.310
It's like we don't learn anything.

908
00:46:51.310 --> 00:46:53.390
- Come on!  - Let's pick it up out there!

909
00:46:53.390 --> 00:46:55.940
Pass! Shoot it! Shoot it!

910
00:46:58.270 --> 00:46:59.900
- That's it!  - No, no, no! Breathe.

911
00:46:59.900 --> 00:47:01.200
Find your happy place.

912
00:47:05.490 --> 00:47:07.000
What's her problem?

913
00:47:13.290 --> 00:47:15.330
- Riley. What's wrong?  - Let's go.

914
00:47:15.330 --> 00:47:17.920
- You're not going to finish try-outs?  - What's the point?

915
00:47:17.920 --> 00:47:20.290
Hey. It'll be all right. Let's just go back...

916
00:47:20.300 --> 00:47:22.440
Stop saying everything will be all right!

917
00:47:24.510 --> 00:47:25.940
Nice hustle, ladies!

918
00:47:34.180 --> 00:47:35.310
Hockey?

919
00:47:38.400 --> 00:47:42.940
No, no, she loves hockey. She can't give up hockey.

920
00:47:42.940 --> 00:47:45.280
Hey! Look at that! Very nice shot!

921
00:47:45.280 --> 00:47:47.240
Bing Bong, we have to get to that station.

922
00:47:47.240 --> 00:47:49.450
Sure thing. This way, just past Graham Cracker Castle.

923
00:47:49.450 --> 00:47:52.700
Hey. That's weird. Graham Cracker Castle used to be right here.

924
00:47:52.700 --> 00:47:55.080
I wonder why they moved it? That's not...

925
00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:57.670
I would have sworn Sparkle Pony Mountain was right here.

926
00:47:57.670 --> 00:47:59.500
- Hey, what's going on?  - Yeah, yeah. I don't know...

927
00:47:59.500 --> 00:48:01.170
- We'll have to come back.  - Princess Dream World!

928
00:48:03.880 --> 00:48:07.010
Oh, no! The Stuffed Animal Hall of Fame!

929
00:48:08.510 --> 00:48:09.600
My rocket!

930
00:48:10.680 --> 00:48:12.510
Wait! Riley and I, we're still using that rocket!

931
00:48:12.510 --> 00:48:15.100
It still has some song power left!

932
00:48:15.100 --> 00:48:16.690
Who's your friend who likes to play?

933
00:48:22.940 --> 00:48:26.900
No! No, no, no. No, you can't take my rocket to the dump!

934
00:48:26.900 --> 00:48:28.280
Riley and I are going to the moon!

935
00:48:34.200 --> 00:48:36.370
Riley can't be done with me.

936
00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:46.130
Hey, it's going to be okay! We can fix this!

937
00:48:46.130 --> 00:48:48.130
We just need to get back to headquarters.

938
00:48:48.130 --> 00:48:49.510
Which way to the train station?

939
00:48:49.510 --> 00:48:52.100
I had a whole trip planned for us.

940
00:48:53.350 --> 00:48:58.070
Hey, who's ticklish, huh? Here comes the tickle monster!

941
00:48:59.390 --> 00:49:00.900
Hey, Bing Bong! Look at this!

942
00:49:03.820 --> 00:49:05.110
Here's a fun game!

943
00:49:05.110 --> 00:49:09.280
You point to the train station and we all go there!

944
00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:12.580
Won't that be fun? Come on, let's go to the train station!

945
00:49:14.160 --> 00:49:16.000
I'm sorry they took your rocket.

946
00:49:16.950 --> 00:49:19.370
They took something that you loved.

947
00:49:19.370 --> 00:49:21.500
It's gone. Forever.

948
00:49:21.500 --> 00:49:23.920
Sadness. Don't make him feel worse.

949
00:49:23.920 --> 00:49:24.700
Sorry.

950
00:49:24.700 --> 00:49:27.210
It's all I had left of Riley.

951
00:49:27.210 --> 00:49:29.970
I bet you and Riley had great adventures.

952
00:49:30.680 --> 00:49:32.180
They were wonderful.

953
00:49:32.180 --> 00:49:36.010
Once we flew back in time. We had breakfast twice that day.

954
00:49:36.010 --> 00:49:37.180
Sadness...

955
00:49:37.180 --> 00:49:39.900
It sounds amazing. I bet Riley liked it.

956
00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:44.610
She did. We were best friends.

957
00:49:44.610 --> 00:49:47.000
Yeah. It's sad.

958
00:49:59.200 --> 00:50:00.790
I'm okay now.

959
00:50:02.170 --> 00:50:05.100
Come on. The train station is this way.

960
00:50:11.510 --> 00:50:13.130
How did you do that?

961
00:50:13.140 --> 00:50:15.140
I don't know. He was sad.

962
00:50:15.140 --> 00:50:16.470
So I listened to what...

963
00:50:16.470 --> 00:50:18.980
Hey! There's the train!

964
00:50:29.280 --> 00:50:32.920
We made it! We're finally going to get home!

965
00:50:34.160 --> 00:50:37.660
Oh, no! These facts and opinions look so similar.

966
00:50:37.660 --> 00:50:40.330
Don't worry about it. Happens all the time.

967
00:50:44.670 --> 00:50:47.290
On a scale of one to ten, I give this day an F.

968
00:50:47.290 --> 00:50:50.420
Well, why don't we quit standing around and do something?

969
00:50:50.420 --> 00:50:51.590
Like what, genius?

970
00:50:51.590 --> 00:50:53.510
Like quitting. That's what I'm doing.

971
00:50:53.510 --> 00:50:57.690
Sure it's the coward's way out. But this coward's gonna survive.

972
00:51:05.350 --> 00:51:07.020
Emotions can't quit, genius!

973
00:51:08.770 --> 00:51:10.900
I thought we were supposed to be keeping Riley happy.

974
00:51:11.440 --> 00:51:13.070
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

975
00:51:18.950 --> 00:51:20.580
- What is it?  - Nothing.

976
00:51:20.580 --> 00:51:22.950
- Just the best idea ever.  - What?

977
00:51:22.960 --> 00:51:25.620
All the good core memories were made in Minnesota.

978
00:51:25.620 --> 00:51:28.790
Ergo, we go back to Minnesota and make more.

979
00:51:28.790 --> 00:51:29.880
- Ta-da!  - Wait, wait, wait.

980
00:51:29.880 --> 00:51:31.880
You're saying we run away?

981
00:51:31.880 --> 00:51:33.340
Well, I wouldn't call it that.

982
00:51:33.340 --> 00:51:36.050
I'd call it the happy core memory development program.

983
00:51:36.050 --> 00:51:37.430
You can't be serious.

984
00:51:37.430 --> 00:51:38.930
Hey! Our life was perfect

985
00:51:38.930 --> 00:51:42.900
until mom and dad decided to move to San Fran stinktown.

986
00:51:43.560 --> 00:51:45.270
I mean, it's just so drastic!

987
00:51:45.270 --> 00:51:47.520
Need I remind you of how great things were there?

988
00:51:47.520 --> 00:51:50.280
Our room? Our back yard? Our friends?

989
00:51:51.980 --> 00:51:53.400
TripleDent Gum will make you smile.

990
00:51:53.400 --> 00:51:55.740
Did I ask for the gum commercial?

991
00:51:56.150 --> 00:51:57.660
Anyway, it was better, that's my point.

992
00:51:57.660 --> 00:52:00.240
Yeah, Riley was happier in Minnesota.

993
00:52:00.240 --> 00:52:02.410
Wait. Hold on. Shouldn't we just sleep on this or something?

994
00:52:02.830 --> 00:52:04.370
Fine. Let's sleep on it.

995
00:52:04.370 --> 00:52:07.330
Because, hey, I'm sure jolly fun-filled times

996
00:52:07.330 --> 00:52:09.800
are just around the corner.

997
00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:23.390
Hey, hey! Why aren't we moving?

998
00:52:23.390 --> 00:52:25.850
Riley's gone to sleep. We're all on break.

999
00:52:25.850 --> 00:52:27.730
You mean we're stuck here until morning?

1000
00:52:27.730 --> 00:52:30.020
Yeah, the train of thought doesn't run while she's asleep.

1001
00:52:30.020 --> 00:52:32.480
- We can't wait that long.  - How about we wake her up?

1002
00:52:32.480 --> 00:52:35.360
Sadness, that's ridiculous! How could we possibly...

1003
00:52:37.700 --> 00:52:38.820
How about we wake her up?

1004
00:52:38.820 --> 00:52:41.450
- Great idea, Joy.  - Thanks. Come on!

1005
00:52:46.790 --> 00:52:48.530
This place is huge!

1006
00:52:48.540 --> 00:52:51.030
Yeah, it looks so much smaller than I expected.

1007
00:52:51.790 --> 00:52:54.700
I can fly? I love that one!

1008
00:52:56.380 --> 00:52:58.450
Rainbow Unicorn! She's right there!

1009
00:53:01.390 --> 00:53:04.470
My friend says you're famous. She wants your autograph.

1010
00:53:04.470 --> 00:53:07.330
No, no, Sadness, don't bother Miss Unicorn, okay?

1011
00:53:07.350 --> 00:53:10.340
Sorry, she's from out of town. That was so embarrassing, right?

1012
00:53:11.560 --> 00:53:13.800
I loved you in Fairy Dream Adventure Part 7.

1013
00:53:13.820 --> 00:53:15.480
Okay, bye. I love you!

1014
00:53:16.740 --> 00:53:18.500
I wonder what that means.

1015
00:53:18.530 --> 00:53:19.750
Well, let's go in.

1016
00:53:21.950 --> 00:53:24.720
Set up the classroom set! Today's memories are in!

1017
00:53:24.740 --> 00:53:26.620
We've got a lot to work with here.

1018
00:53:26.660 --> 00:53:28.680
Riley dumped her best friend,

1019
00:53:28.680 --> 00:53:29.670
had a miserable day at school,

1020
00:53:29.710 --> 00:53:30.790
and quit hockey.

1021
00:53:30.790 --> 00:53:33.050
The writers have put together a killer script!

1022
00:53:33.090 --> 00:53:35.290
Just because Joy and Sadness are gone,

1023
00:53:35.300 --> 00:53:36.940
I have to do stupid dream duty.

1024
00:53:38.550 --> 00:53:40.690
Okay. How are we going to wake her up?

1025
00:53:40.720 --> 00:53:43.640
Well, she wakes up sometimes when she has a scary dream.

1026
00:53:43.640 --> 00:53:44.690
We could scare her.

1027
00:53:44.720 --> 00:53:47.020
Scare her? No, she's been through enough already.

1028
00:53:47.060 --> 00:53:48.140
- But, Joy...  - Sadness,

1029
00:53:48.140 --> 00:53:49.640
you may know your way around down here,

1030
00:53:49.640 --> 00:53:50.690
but I know Riley.

1031
00:53:50.730 --> 00:53:54.250
We're gonna make her so happy, she'll wake up with exhilaration.

1032
00:53:54.270 --> 00:53:55.610
We'll excite her awake!

1033
00:53:55.610 --> 00:53:57.750
That's never happened before.

1034
00:53:57.780 --> 00:53:59.420
Riley loves dogs. Put this on.

1035
00:53:59.440 --> 00:54:00.490
I don't think that'll work.

1036
00:54:00.490 --> 00:54:02.210
- Bing Bong?  - Yeah?

1037
00:54:02.240 --> 00:54:05.340
- Don't let anything happen to these.  - Got it.

1038
00:54:06.580 --> 00:54:08.800
Add the reality distortion filter.

1039
00:54:10.790 --> 00:54:13.710
Love it. Remember, play to the camera, everyone!

1040
00:54:13.750 --> 00:54:15.420
Riley is the camera!

